WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.024 --> 00:00:07.456
What is the world’s most popular drink? What drink has played an important role in the world’s history, politics, and religion?

2
00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:10.234
What drink is over five thousand years old?

3
00:00:10.235 --> 00:00:19.407
The answer is tea, and its story begins with Chinese Emperor Shen Nung, a scholar and scientist who lived over five thousand years ago.

4
00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:25.455
The emperor had ruled that throughout his kingdom all drinking water must be boiled as a hygienic precaution.

5
00:00:25.456 --> 00:00:32.601
One day while visiting a distant region, the emperor stopped to rest, and the servants began to boil water for everyone to drink.

6
00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:38.348
At this moment, the wind blew and some dried leaves from a nearby bush fell into the boiling water.

7
00:00:38.349 --> 00:00:40.301
The liquid became brown.

8
00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:46.482
As a scientist, the emperor was interested in the new liquid, drank some, and found it very refreshing.

9
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:52.701
The tree was a wild tea tree. And so, according to legend, tea was created.

10
00:00:52.702 --> 00:00:56.590
From ancient times tea was renowned as a healthy, refreshing drink.

11
00:00:56.591 --> 00:01:01.126
The first detailed description of tea was written in 350 AD.

12
00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:05.316
Fresh, green tea leaves were picked, then pressed into hard "bricks."

13
00:01:05.317 --> 00:01:11.133
These bricks were roasted, crumbled into water, and boiled with onion, ginger, and orange.

14
00:01:11.134 --> 00:01:18.285
It was not until the Tang Dynasty that tea became China’s national drink and the word "cha" was used to describe tea.

15
00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:24.393
The first book on tea, called Cha Ching , was written by Lu Yu in 780 AD.

16
00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:29.567
It had three volumes and described tea cultivation and preparation in ancient China.

17
00:01:29.568 --> 00:01:36.733
The modern term "tea" derives from words such as tchai, cha , and tay in early Chinese

18
00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.947
dialects. Its botanical name is Camellia

19
00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:44.438
sinensis . Tea is an evergreen plant with smooth, shiny,

20
00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:49.548
pointed leaves. After China, the first two countries to adopt tea were its neighbors, Korea

21
00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:56.697
and Japan. Tea first came to Korea during the Unified Shilla Dynasty, between 57 BC and

22
00:01:56.698 --> 00:02:01.655
935 AD. As it was in China, tea was used for social and religious purposes

23
00:02:01.656 --> 00:02:08.909
in Korea. Tea was drunk socially among the royal family and aristocrats, and Buddhist monks drank tea to help them stay awake

24
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.306
during meditation. Tea drinking became widespread in the

25
00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:19.514
Goryo Dynasty. During this time, special ceramic cups and bowls for tea drinking were designed, and an elaborate tea ceremony

26
00:02:19.515 --> 00:02:26.781
was developed. The ceremony begins with pouring the boiling water into a bowl, where it stands until it cools to about 60

27
00:02:26.782 --> 00:02:30.026
degrees Celsius. If the water is too hot, the tea will be

28
00:02:30.027 --> 00:02:35.772
too bitter. The teapot and cups are warmed with some of the water, and then the tea leaves are warmed in

29
00:02:35.773 --> 00:02:40.391
the teapot. Then, the water is poured into the teapot and left to brew for two or

30
00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:46.659
three minutes. When the tea is poured, each cup is filled little by little so that the taste is evenly distributed in all

31
00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:58.139
the cups. The tea must be sipped slowly, and as you sip, you must think about the four characteristics of tea according to Korean Buddhism: peacefulness, respectfulness, purity,

32
00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:06.180
and quietness. During the Joseon Dynasty, Confucianism replaced Buddhism as the court religion, and wine replaced tea as the

33
00:03:06.181 --> 00:03:10.640
favored drink. Tea went out of fashion and was not revived until five hundred

34
00:03:10.641 --> 00:03:17.362
years later. Tea was introduced to Japan in 1191 by Yeisei, "The Father of Tea," a traveling

35
00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:23.697
Buddhist monk. As in Korea, tea was first used by Buddhist monks and aristocrats, and then spread to the rest

36
00:03:23.698 --> 00:03:27.634
of society. By this time, tea was no longer served in "cakes" but

37
00:03:27.635 --> 00:03:31.515
was powdered. Tea became so popular that even a tea guessing game

38
00:03:31.516 --> 00:03:40.620
was played. Beginning in early morning and continuing well into evening, guests would sample as many as fifty varieties of tea, trying to guess their places

39
00:03:40.621 --> 00:03:45.239
of origin. From the fourteenth to sixteenth centuries, a Japanese tea ritual

40
00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:53.440
was developed. The Japanese tea ceremony takes place in a special room designed for tea drinking and consists of many small rituals that have to be learned by

41
00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:59.121
heart. It is much more elaborate than the Korean ceremony, and almost every hand movement is

42
00:03:59.122 --> 00:04:02.177
prescribed. Tea didn’t reach Europe until the fifteenth

43
00:04:02.178 --> 00:04:07.041
century. As the Europeans increased their trade with China, rumors of a new substance

44
00:04:07.042 --> 00:04:10.817
circulated. When tea finally arrived, people were unsure how to use

45
00:04:10.818 --> 00:04:15.646
it. One writer suggested that tea leaves be boiled, salted, buttered, and

46
00:04:15.647 --> 00:04:20.261
eaten! Some doctors and scholars also warned that this strange dark liquid was

47
00:04:20.262 --> 00:04:24.409
unhealthy. In reality, tea drinking actually increased the health of people in

48
00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:29.810
Europe. Water was too dangerous to drink at the time, so people drank beer at breakfast, lunch, and

49
00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:35.467
dinner! Tea, made with boiled and therefore safe water, was a vast improvement in the European

50
00:04:35.468 --> 00:04:41.228
diet. Nowadays, black tea is Britain’s national drink, but Britons were the last Europeans to adopt

51
00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:48.061
it. Within fifty years, however, tea became so popular in Britain that Britain was the largest tea importer in

52
00:04:48.062 --> 00:04:53.274
Europe. Over the next few centuries, tea played a major role in world history and

53
00:04:53.275 --> 00:04:56.616
politics. European companies bought tea from China and

54
00:04:56.617 --> 00:05:03.271
India. The East India Company, in fact, became so rich and powerful that it ruled the nation of India for several

55
00:05:03.272 --> 00:05:09.819
years. This British company forced Indian workers to produce the drug opium, which was sold to China in exchange for

56
00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:20.587
tea. In the 1800s, England was the largest drug trafficking organization in the world, and was responsible for a devastating drug addiction problem in China—all just to control the trade in

57
00:05:20.588 --> 00:05:24.465
tea. In the new colony of America, tea was also causing

58
00:05:24.466 --> 00:05:32.685
trouble. In 1773, in a famous incident called the Boston Tea Party, 340 chests of tea were emptied into the

59
00:05:32.686 --> 00:05:42.245
ocean. Residents of Boston were protesting against the same company, the East India Company, and their protest was one of the first incidents that led to the American

60
00:05:42.246 --> 00:05:48.788
Revolution. In the nineteenth century, tea led to the creation of two new meal times: "morning tea" and "afternoon

61
00:05:48.789 --> 00:05:55.288
tea." A woman who managed a bread shop in England convinced her bosses to allow her to serve tea to her favorite

62
00:05:55.289 --> 00:06:00.614
customers. The shop set up some tables in 1864 and a new form of socializing was

63
00:06:00.615 --> 00:06:06.954
born. As one famous author said, "For the English, afternoon tea is really a picnic

64
00:06:06.955 --> 00:06:12.056
indoors." Morning tea and afternoon tea are still common in Britain and Commonwealth

65
00:06:12.057 --> 00:06:20.149
countries. Iced green tea was served with alcohol in the United States in the 1800s, but it was not until 1904 that iced tea really took

66
00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:23.869
off. At the World’s Fair, hot tea was given away free for

67
00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.756
guests. Because of the intense heat, ice was added to the tea and it became an instant hit!

68
00:06:28.757 --> 00:06:33.312
Today, iced tea is usually made with lemon and sweetened with sugar.

69
00:06:33.313 --> 00:06:37.800
Nowadays, tea comes in green, black, and oolong varieties.

70
00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:46.456
Europeans and Americans have traditionally favored black teas, Asians prefer green tea, and Indians and East Asians drink a spiced tea called chai.

71
00:06:46.457 --> 00:06:53.629
However, the health benefits of green tea, including reducing the risks of cancer, are increasing its popularity worldwide.

72
00:06:53.630 --> 00:07:01.179
Herbal "tea," sometimes called a tisane or an infusion, is made by infusing herbs other than the tea plant in hot water.

73
00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.829
Hundreds of different kinds of herbal tea are drunk around the world.

74
00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:10.007
Some of the most popular are chamomile, mint, rosehip, and ginger.

75
00:07:10.008 --> 00:07:18.620
Many blends of real tea are prepared by adding other plants; for example, the popular Earl Grey tea is black tea infused with bergamot.

76
00:07:18.621 --> 00:07:22.556
Tea has been a part of human culture since the earliest written records.

77
00:07:22.557 --> 00:07:27.717
It has shaped societies, started wars, and changed the course of history.

78
00:07:27.718 --> 00:07:29.868
All because of a simple drink!

79
00:07:29.869 --> 00:07:44.533
William Gladstone, the prime minister of England, summed it up nicely: "If you are cold, tea will warm you; if you are too heated; it will cool you; if you are depressed, it will cheer you; if you are exhausted, it will calm you."

